    <imageSet>
        <name>Complete set of subtomograms for Rubisco subtomogram average</name>
        <directory>/data</directory>
        <category>picked particles - multiframe - unprocessed</category>
        <headerFormat>MRC</headerFormat>
        <dataFormat>MRC</dataFormat>
        <numImagesOrTiltSeries>32930</numImagesOrTiltSeries>
        <framesPerImage>1</framesPerImage>
        <voxelType>32 BIT FLOAT</voxelType>
        <dimensions>
            <imageWidth>160</imageWidth>
            <pixelWidth>1.104</pixelWidth>
            <imageHeight>160</imageHeight>
            <pixelHeight>1.104</pixelHeight>
        </dimensions>
        <details>subtomograms.tar.gz contains the complete set of Rubisco subtomograms from the purified alpha-carboxysome dataset. The file pattern is subtomograms/particle_*.mrc, and the picked particles file is subtomograms/particles.csv. Subtomograms were cropped in Dynamo from from bin1 WBP tomograms reconstructed in novaCTF. The particles.csv text file contains position and orientation information for each subtomogram, as well as defocus, carboxysome number, cross-correlation coefficient, and other data to allow users to import subtomograms into the software package of their choice. A detailed description of the csv information is in the csvColumnDefinitions.txt file, also in the subtomograms directory.</details>
        <segmentationList/>
        <micrographsFilePattern></micrographsFilePattern>
        <pickedParticlesFilePattern></pickedParticlesFilePattern>
        <pickedParticlesDirectory></pickedParticlesDirectory>
    </imageSet>
